  "description": "Captures precarity photographed as landscape. After the factory that was her Nevada town closes — the town itself is dissolved — a widowed woman in her sixties joins the van-dwelling seasonal workforce: Amazon warehouses at Christmas, beet harvests, desert gatherings of people living the same arithmetic. Zhao films real nomads as themselves; the near future here is not a gadget but a retirement with no floor under it.\n\nAfter losing everything in the Great Recession, a woman in her sixties embarks on a journey through the American West, living as a van-dwelling nomad.",
